                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e467bd2a-6dfe-49be-b388-33f8e73c0af9",
                                                "sense_id": "aa18cfb5-1aae-390c-9172-94c462e15d15",
                                                "text": "The three subordinates on whom President Roosevelt depends to win his Senate victories are Majority Leader Joseph T. Robinson of Arkansas, the bull-voiced, heavy-fisted field commander; Pat Harrison of Mississippi, the shrewd committee and cloakroom horsetrader; and James F. Byrnes of South Carolina."
                                            }
